# Runbook — field exposure environment flags

```yaml
runbook_version: "2026-06-29-v1"
map_ref: docs/architecture/field-exposure-system.md
```

## Flags

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| -------- | ------- | ------- |
| `FIELD_EXPOSURE_RUNTIME_MODE` | `legacy` | Runtime truth source: `legacy` \| `shadow` \| `engine` — controls forward delivery field selection |
| `FIELD_EXPOSURE_ENGINE_FAIL_CLOSED` | unset / `false` | When `true`, skip integration enqueue if exposure selector fails (9.10) |
| `FIELD_EXPOSURE_CONSISTENCY_GATE_FATAL` | unset / `false` | When `true`, missing exposure DB tables block integration mutations (9.1b) |

## Safe rollout order

```text
1. Deploy code + migrations (exposure_intents, exposure_profiles, reminder activations)
2. prisma generate + API restart
3. Observe metrics (fail-closed false)
4. Staging: FIELD_EXPOSURE_CONSISTENCY_GATE_FATAL=true
5. Staging: FIELD_EXPOSURE_ENGINE_FAIL_CLOSED=true
6. Production: same after parity tests green (test:exposure:integration)
```

## Runtime mode notes

- **`legacy`** — delivery field ids from integration policy / legacy mapper (production default during migration).
- **`shadow`** — engine runs in parallel; legacy still authoritative for enqueue.
- **`engine`** — engine authoritative; requires parity gate sign-off (Phase 6+ cutover).

Changing `FIELD_EXPOSURE_RUNTIME_MODE` without staging validation can change Telegram field sets — treat as **product-visible** change.

